          "The conversation's own Linux machine, with Node 24, npm and git. Commands start in /tmp/conexus-git-conexus_test_<id-1>/conexus-machine-<id-2>/app, the app folder: work there and nowhere else. Its network reaches only registry.npmjs.org. Conexus keeps its check in /opt/conexus, read only: run it with the tool conexus_check, never by hand.",
          "",
          "Files are stored in a remote sandbox at /tmp/conexus-git-conexus_test_<id-1>/conexus-machine-<id-2>/app. File tools take paths relative to /tmp/conexus-git-conexus_test_<id-1>/conexus-machine-<id-2>/app, or absolute paths under it. Any other absolute path is placed inside /tmp/conexus-git-conexus_test_<id-1>/conexus-machine-<id-2>/app (/tmp/x becomes /tmp/conexus-git-conexus_test_<id-1>/conexus-machine-<id-2>/app/tmp/x), while commands see the real path: keep every file a tool and a command share under /tmp/conexus-git-conexus_test_<id-1>/conexus-machine-<id-2>/app."
